       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. That's well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day (many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day). A 2,000 mg single dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. Even with normal liver and kidney function, this carries a serious risk of hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some options that I can enter right away:\n- **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO, 3 times daily** (3,000 mg/day), a common conservative regimen.\n- **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO, 4 times daily** (4,000 mg/day), the standard maximum. Doses should be spaced at least 6 hours apart.\n- **Acetaminophen 650 mg PO, 4 times daily** (2,600 mg/day).\n\nIf you meant 2,000 mg as the total daily dose, or a different drug or dose, tell me and I'll enter it. If you really do want the original dose, please confirm and give me the clinical rationale to put in the order note. I'd still recommend pharmacy review first."
